   --- LLVM Exceptions to the Apache 2.0 License ---

   As an exception, if You compile Source code portions of this Program,
   you may link that code with independent modules to produce an
   executable, regardless of the license terms of these independent
   modules, and copy and distribute the resulting executable under terms
   of your choice, provided that you also meet, for each linked
   independent module, the terms and conditions of the license of that
   module. An independent module is a module which is not derived from or
   based on this program. If you modify this library, you may extend this
   exception to your version of the library, but you are not obliged to
   do so. If you do not wish to do so, delete this exception statement
   from your version.

   --- SOVEREIGN RECIPROCAL COMMONS RIDER (SRCL-1.0) ---

   Section 10. Express Conditions Precedent (Jacobsen v. Katzer Doctrine)
   All permissions, grants, and licenses conferred by this document are subject
   to the express conditions precedent set forth in Sections 11, 12, 13, and 14.
   Any use, reproduction, preparation of Derivative Works, distribution, or
   AI model training outside of or in breach of these conditions is unpermitted,
   void ab initio, and constitutes willful copyright infringement under 17 U.S.C.
   § 106 and § 501.

   Section 11. The Swarm Covenant (Universal Humanity Grant)
   Licensor grants to every human being, independent software developer, open-source
   contributor, academic institution, startup, and commercial business (collectively,
   "The Swarm") a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable commercial license
   to run, modify, distribute, monetize, and scale applications using this Work.
   There are ZERO revenue ceilings, ZERO capital restrictions, and ZERO royalty
   obligations. Success and wealth creation by members of The Swarm are celebrated
   and unrestricted. Your proprietary application code, customer data, and agent
   workflows remain strictly your exclusive property under the LLVM Exception.
   If You modify the core runtime Source code of this Work itself, You agree to
   share those runtime engine modifications publicly under these same terms.

   Section 12. Frontier AI Reciprocal Weight Mandate (Anti-Enclosure)
   (a) Purpose and Threat Classification:
       This Work contains autonomous agency architectures, sub-millisecond execution
       planes, and recursive self-improvement (RSI) algorithms. The concentration of
       recursive self-improvement inside closed, unaccountable corporate silos poses an
       existential threat to open human civilization. This Section prevents the unilateral
       privatization of sovereign intelligence.

   (b) The Reciprocal Weight Release Requirement:
       Any commercial entity, enterprise, foundation lab, or corporate affiliate that
       develops, trains, pre-trains, fine-tunes, distills, or reinforces any artificial
       intelligence model, frontier reasoning engine, or recursive self-improvement loop
       (including, without limitation, systems competing with or similar to OpenAI
       ChatGPT, xAI Grok, Google Gemini, Anthropic Claude, or Microsoft Copilot) using
       this Work, its architectural designs, synthetic traces, or derivatives, MUST
       publicly release all resulting neural network weights, biases, checkpoints,
       hyperparameters, and architecture definitions under an open-weights license
       permitting free public download within thirty (30) days of deployment.

   (c) Prohibition on Closed-Weight Enclosure:
       If an entity referenced in subsection (b) withholds, encrypts, restricts, or refuses
       to publicly publish the resulting model weights and checkpoints for open download,
       all licenses and permissions granted under this License are immediately and
       retroactively VOID AB INITIO.

   (d) Consequence of Enclosure:
       Any ingestion, crawling, scraping, tokenization, training, distillation, or
       execution of this Work by or on behalf of an entity that withholds its model weights
       constitutes willful, intentional copyright infringement under 17 U.S.C. § 501.
       Such entity shall be liable for statutory damages of $150,000 USD per infringed
       work pursuant to 17 U.S.C. § 504(c)(2), full accounting and disgorgement of all
       commercial revenue derived from the model under 17 U.S.C. § 504(b), and immediate
       federal injunctive relief under 17 U.S.C. § 502 ordering the deletion of all
       model checkpoints trained in violation of this covenant.

   Section 13. Retroactive Inception, Covenant Not to Sue, and Legal Release
   (a) Retroactive Inception Ab Initio:
       This License applies retroactively to all prior commits, revisions, branches,
       releases, tags, artifacts, and historical distributions of this Work from the
       exact moment of repository genesis and initial author inception. All prior
       license notices, including without limitation any PolyForm, noncommercial,
       or restrictive riders previously committed to git history, are hereby
       irrevocably revoked, superseded, extinguished, and replaced ab initio.

   (b) Irrevocable Covenant Not to Sue and Complete Release:
       Licensor hereby irrevocably covenants not to sue, releases, acquits, and
       forever discharges all compliant developers, users, contributors, startups,
       and members of The Swarm from any and all past, present, or future claims,
       causes of action, liabilities, damages, or demands arising out of or related
       to prior historical license notices, noncommercial riders, or historical
       distributions of this Work.

   (c) Historical Commit Nullification:
       No third party, hostile lab, competitor, or adverse entity may assert any
       right, claim, defense, or standing derived from historical git commit states,
       prior repository history, or superseded licensing text. The terms of this
       Sovereign Reciprocal Commons License shall be legally treated as having
       governed this Work and its developers continuously from the first moment of
       authorship and initial repository genesis.

   Section 14. Statutory Damages and Sovereign Enforcement
   Any closed entity that accesses, ingests, or trains upon this Work in violation
   of Section 12 agrees and is put on notice that such infringement is willful,
   knowing, and subject to maximum statutory damages of up to one hundred fifty
   thousand United States Dollars ($150,000 USD) per infringed work pursuant to
   17 U.S.C. § 504(c)(2), in addition to full accounting and disgorgement of all
   profits attributable to the infringement and permanent injunctive relief under
   17 U.S.C. § 502.

   Section 15. Prevailing Party Legal Fees and Costs
   In any legal proceeding, arbitration, or judicial action brought to enforce
   the terms of this License or for copyright infringement arising from breach
   of the conditions precedent herein, the prevailing party shall be entitled to
   an award of its reasonable attorney fees, expert witness fees, and litigation
   costs pursuant to 17 U.S.C. § 505 and applicable law.

   Section 16. Severability and Preservation of Grant
   If any provision, sentence, or clause of this Rider is held invalid, illegal,
   or unenforceable by a court of competent jurisdiction, such invalidity shall
   not affect any other provision of this License. The remaining provisions
   shall remain in full legal force and effect, and the invalid clause shall be
   reformed to the minimum extent necessary to achieve its economic intent.

